Hi Parth I am Berkmans Clinton from Aequor. We have an immediate contract (W2) opportunity for a **Cage Wash Technician** with a large Pharma company in **Lawrenceville, NJ-08648-(100% Onsite).** Please find the details below. If this interests you, please share your updated resume with [berkmans.clinton@aequor.com](mailto:berkmans.clinton@aequor.com) or call me @ **+1 609-608-0589** for further details. **Refer your friend or a candidate for this role, and if they get and accept the job, Aequor promises to pay a referral bonus of $500-$1,000. ** **REFER & create a WIN-WIN, ** **Job ID: 62356-1** **Position: Cage Wash Technician** **Location: Lawrenceville, NJ-08648-(100% Onsite)** **Duration: 3+ months with possible extension** **work hours Monday through Friday, 6:30 am to 3:00 pm** **Work Dimensions** * The temporary cage wash/logistic technician will routinely perform the work described in Veterinary Sciences departmental Standard Operating Procedures. * Clean and sterilize animal cages, feeders, bottles, and other equipment using autoclaves and other sanitization equipment, and assist in planning workflow priorities and staging of materials. Clean empty animal rooms and maintain general cleanliness of the animal quarters and ancillary spaces. May be required to perform minor assembly of equipment, lubricate equipment and make minor adjustments and repairs to cages and other equipment, as needed, using hand tools if required. Record the readings of machine function indicators such as temperature tapes, autoclave test ampoules, etc. Receive and store feed, bedding and other supplies. Keep storage and animal areas stocked, as needed. Assemble, clean, use, and pack transfer carts. Must be in compliance with all regulatory guidelines and SOPs. Reporting all errors promptly to their supervisor. * Moderate physical effort required. May involve intermittent heavy lifting. * Medical screening prior to initial placement in Veterinary Sciences is required to evaluate for history of allergy, asthma or physical problems which could endanger an employee in this work environment. * The employee will have frequent exposure to biohazards and disagreeable conditions, including odors, heat, noise, animal excrement and will have potential exposure to toxic test compounds. **Education** * Must have a high school diploma or equivalent. **Thanks & Regards, ** **Berkmans Clinton E** **Senior Technical Recruiter** **O** +1 (609)-608-0589 **E** [berkmans.clinton@aequor.com](mailto:berkmans.clinton@aequor.com) **W** <https://www.aequor.com/> [](https://shared.outlook.inky.com/link?domain=https&t=h.eJxNjcsOgjAURH- FdG3aQkvvhRW_cvtACYVihZBo_HdTN7qaZObkzIsdObK- Yrd933ohSjzEeZ6cwv1Imbu0CHap2FygNewpX7WWbQONGOk5xcGlGMlO65i-bOic0YoCdBY0SjV6Qmk0WpRoEJyoTScVANYtB13MoZgXyjO3gbIffsdl9WX9q94fTv418A.MEMCIDl371vOjs_S1VBLhobcDr6Fi_9oFYoIwptU4iSQ_Lm8Ah8hNV8XOmK_rJvDAWFEaYhnibUtheUazGB8q3Xlwbhx) --- **Connect | Collaborate | Succeed!** You have received this message because either you have contacted our Company to express interest in employment, or you have posted your Resume in an area accessible to recruiters or HR professionals, which implies an interest in being contacted regarding employment opportunities. If you no longer wish to receive any emails from our Company, you can withdraw your consent at any time by clicking [unsubscribe](https://www1.joboppforyou.com/optout.jsp?d=3134355f706161727468706174656c3139393840676d61696c2e636f6d&e=148&t11=1747318332434).

